 Readiness and opening speech precede reveal and are deliberately excluded from active search time. The system will also retain the broader interval from opening-cue onset to selection. This measure includes the opening instruction, whose duration may differ across voices, while active completion time remains the primary outcome.
 
-A stopped or timed-out trial has an observed duration and an outcome reason, but it does not have a successful completion time, and the analysis must not copy its stop timestamp into a success field. Source and receipt timestamps are likewise kept distinct, because a file that arrives late in the viewer reflects a transfer delay rather than necessarily a delay in the headset event.
+A stopped or timed-out trial has an observed duration and an outcome reason, but it does not have a successful completion time, and the analysis must not copy its stop timestamp into a success field. In the October 23 deadline implementation, a timeout records 15 seconds of active search exposure, a distinct timeout event, and an unsuccessful outcome. Software observes expiry on an update, while the exposure clock is capped at the deadline; event timestamps retain the actual observation time. Earlier development recordings retain their original durations and must not be retrospectively truncated to this limit. Source and receipt timestamps are likewise kept distinct, because a file that arrives late in the viewer reflects a transfer delay rather than necessarily a delay in the headset event.
 
 Recent conversational AR research shows why the definition must be explicit: Madritsch et al. distinguish overall task-completion time from active working time in an assistant-supported procedural task~\cite{madritsch2026assistance}, and their active measure is not assumed to correspond to the present clock. In Follow My Voice, active completion time includes ordinary waits for guidance between object reveal and correct selection, and only recorded pauses are excluded. Separate decision and playback timestamps will therefore help explain delivery delays without removing their task-level consequences from the primary outcome.
 
