 Tracking loss can affect guidance and measurement simultaneously, though not always in the same way. A trial with sparse gaze coverage may have valid selection timing yet unreliable gaze-contact latency, so exclusion should be measure-specific where justified. A missing gaze contact does not automatically invalidate completion time, and a complete motion stream does not repair missing voice playback events. Each analysis will therefore report its own denominator and reasons for missingness.
 
-Stopping, timeout, withdrawal, and technical failure require a prespecified treatment. A complete-case time model estimates completion times among observed successful trials under its assumptions, and it may not describe all assigned trials if incomplete outcomes differ by voice. The final plan must therefore also define a complementary completion-probability or time-to-event analysis for use if incompletion is consequential. The source protocol does not yet specify a timeout threshold, and none is assumed here.
+Stopping, timeout, withdrawal, and technical failure require a prespecified treatment. A complete-case time model estimates completion times among observed successful trials under its assumptions, and it may not describe all assigned trials if incomplete outcomes differ by voice. The final plan must therefore also define a complementary completion-probability or time-to-event analysis for use if incompletion is consequential. The revised protocol fixes the active-search deadline at 15 seconds. Deadline-expired attempts are unsuccessful outcomes for completion probability and right-censored at 15 active seconds for a time-to-event analysis; they are not successful 15-second completion times. Earlier development recordings predate this rule and retain their original exposure.
 
-Raw attempts, incorrect selections, pause intervals, timeouts, technical failures and withdrawals will all be retained, and stopped trials will not be coded as successful completion times. Timeout and censoring rules, together with the missing-data estimand, will be specified before collection so that slow trials are not removed solely for being slow. Missing responses will not be replaced with zero; questionnaire scores will instead follow the complete-subscale rule, with item-level missingness reported.
+Raw attempts, incorrect selections, pause intervals, timeouts, technical failures and withdrawals will all be retained, and stopped trials will not be coded as successful completion times. The deadline outcome is recorded separately from technical failure and withdrawal. The remaining treatment of those interruptions and the missing-data estimand will be specified before collection; slow successful trials within the deadline are not removed solely for being slow. Missing responses will not be replaced with zero; questionnaire scores will instead follow the complete-subscale rule, with item-level missingness reported.
 
 \subsection{Behavior as Outcome Rather Than Automatic Adjustment}
 Instruction count, gaze path, and controller behavior can be consequences of voice condition. Including them automatically as primary-model covariates could remove part of the effect the study intends to estimate. The primary comparison therefore adjusts for pre-cue difficulty and design variables. Voice-by-theta variation, selected neutral voice, acoustic quality, guidance timing, and search behavior will enter exploratory or sensitivity analyses with their assumptions reported.
